This product includes software developed as part of, or derived from:

  * ChatTS — https://github.com/NetmanAIOps/ChatTS (Apache-2.0)
    The time-series alignment dataset and the patch-based encoder design
    follow ChatTS (Xie et al., 2025).

  * ChatTS-Training — https://github.com/xiezhe-24/ChatTS-Training (Apache-2.0)
    The two-stage SFT training stack (`chatts` template + time-series encoder
    integration on top of LLaMA-Factory) is built on ChatTS-Training. It is
    included here as a git submodule under third_party/ChatTS-Training.

  * LLaMA-Factory — https://github.com/hiyouga/LLaMA-Factory (Apache-2.0)
    The TS-Text-FT text-only baseline is fine-tuned with LLaMA-Factory.

  * The `align_256`, `align_random`, and `ift` data channels used for
    encoder alignment and instruction following originate from the ChatTS
    public release; see third_party/ChatTS-Training and the ChatTS repo for
    their terms.

Study data: The passive-sensing and EMA data underlying the paper were
collected under NIH/NIMH award R01MH123482-01 and are governed by IRB and
funder data-use restrictions. They are NOT included in this repository. Only
synthetic, schema-faithful fake data (data/fake/) is shipped here. De-identified
study data is the responsibility of the NIMH NDA archive (https://nda.nih.gov).
